1
00:00:04,833 --> 00:00:11,833
[THEME MUSIC PLAYING]

2
00:00:31,467 --> 00:00:33,200
[TIRES SCREECHING]

3
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:35,533
[ENGINE REVVING]

4
00:00:39,867 --> 00:00:41,333
[TIRES SCREECH]

5
00:00:42,133 --> 00:00:43,967
[ENGINE REVVING]

6
00:00:44,100 --> 00:00:45,200
[TRUCK HORN BLARES]

7
00:00:45,333 --> 00:00:46,567
[LOUD CRASH]

8
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:48,900
[TIRES SCREECHING]

9
00:00:50,000 --> 00:00:51,333
<i>- Stop!
- [GUNSHOT]</i>

10
00:00:52,300 --> 00:00:53,567
[FIREWORKS EXPLODING]

11
00:00:53,700 --> 00:00:55,533
- [ENGINE REVVING]
- [BUS HORN HONKS]

12
00:00:56,500 --> 00:00:57,933
[GLASS SHATTERING]

13
00:00:58,067 --> 00:01:00,400
- [TIRES SCREECHING]
- [LOUD CRASH]

14
00:01:00,533 --> 00:01:03,233
[ENGINE REVVING]

15
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:06,533
[TIRES SCREECHING]

16
00:01:07,100 --> 00:01:09,300
[TIRES SCREECHING]

17
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,733
- [GUNSHOTS]
- [TIRES SCREECHING]

18
00:01:11,867 --> 00:01:13,000
- [TRUCK HORN HONKS]
- [LOUD CRASH]

19
00:01:13,133 --> 00:01:15,000
[TIRES SCREECHING]

20
00:01:19,733 --> 00:01:22,300
<i> Whoever saved Salvador</i>

21
00:01:22,433 --> 00:01:25,733
<i>is the reason why we're
in this trouble right now!</i>

22
00:01:25,867 --> 00:01:28,500
<i> Find out who he is.</i>

23
00:01:28,633 --> 00:01:31,467
<i>Deborah and I are going
to the NCIA.</i>

24
00:01:32,000 --> 00:01:34,000
<i> Colonel Mariano Zafra.</i>

25
00:01:34,133 --> 00:01:35,867
<i>His son is requesting
your presence.</i>

26
00:01:36,933 --> 00:01:39,067
<i>- Mariano.
- Delgado.</i>

27
00:01:39,200 --> 00:01:41,200
<i>I didn't know
you were still serving.</i>

28
00:01:41,367 --> 00:01:42,967
<i>I'm not surprised
that Victor is your son.</i>

29
00:01:43,100 --> 00:01:44,667
<i>The apple doesn't fall
far from the tree</i>

30
00:01:44,800 --> 00:01:46,467
<i>You're disciplining
your favorite agent.</i>

31
00:01:47,167 --> 00:01:48,367
<i> She's not my favorite.</i>

32
00:01:48,500 --> 00:01:50,467
<i> Samantha made a mistake,</i>

33
00:01:50,600 --> 00:01:53,067
<i>and she will be held
accountable for it.</i>

34
00:01:53,200 --> 00:01:54,700
<i>- Django!
- Gabo.</i>

35
00:01:54,833 --> 00:01:57,300
<i>You really won't leave
the poor alone, won't you?</i>

36
00:01:58,300 --> 00:01:59,400
<i> What do you guys want?</i>

37
00:02:00,233 --> 00:02:01,667
<i>Do you want us to wipe
each other out here?!</i>

38
00:02:05,367 --> 00:02:06,400
[PIA] Sir!

39
00:02:09,067 --> 00:02:11,600
Sir, we don't have grounds
to stop them

40
00:02:11,733 --> 00:02:13,767
from talking to Victor Zafra.

41
00:02:14,433 --> 00:02:17,000
Hmm.
That's refreshing.

42
00:02:18,000 --> 00:02:21,100
At least not everyone
at NCIA

43
00:02:22,633 --> 00:02:24,367
has a crooked way of thinking.

44
00:02:26,967 --> 00:02:28,600
You can talk to Victor.

45
00:02:29,767 --> 00:02:33,400
But I have my eyes on you.

46
00:02:33,533 --> 00:02:37,467
Your words don't scare me.

47
00:02:39,400 --> 00:02:41,233
Sir, it's not worth it.

48
00:02:41,367 --> 00:02:48,067
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

49
00:02:48,233 --> 00:02:51,667
Thank you for
your warm welcome, Delgado!

50
00:02:52,133 --> 00:02:53,867
It's definitely warm.

51
00:02:57,167 --> 00:02:59,400
[PIA] Bring them to Victor.

52
00:02:59,533 --> 00:03:01,267
[AGENT] Yes, ma'am.
Let's go.

53
00:03:01,400 --> 00:03:08,367
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

54
00:03:15,333 --> 00:03:16,533
[SEBASTIAN] Sam.

55
00:03:17,000 --> 00:03:18,767
Let's hour together.
I'll drive.

56
00:03:19,200 --> 00:03:20,733
No, Karen is with me.

57
00:03:20,900 --> 00:03:24,533
Oh, you miss her already?
I can move to the back.

58
00:03:24,667 --> 00:03:27,100
No need. We'll go
to the same place anyway.

59
00:03:27,233 --> 00:03:28,367
Let's just meet there.

60
00:03:28,500 --> 00:03:29,667
- Ah--
- Let's go.

61
00:03:29,800 --> 00:03:31,200
[SAM] Let's go,

62
00:03:34,633 --> 00:03:36,433
[MAN] Wake up, Zafra.

63
00:03:36,567 --> 00:03:38,767
[CLATTERING]

64
00:03:41,267 --> 00:03:48,267
[UNEASY MUSIC PLAYING]

65
00:03:49,733 --> 00:03:51,000
[HANDCUFF CLICKS]

66
00:03:52,200 --> 00:03:53,633
[CELL DOOR CREAKS]

67
00:03:55,600 --> 00:03:56,700
[HANDCUFF CLICKS]

68
00:03:56,833 --> 00:04:03,867
[UNEASY MUSIC CONTINUES]

69
00:04:07,167 --> 00:04:09,067
[DEBORAH] Attorney,
you can leave us.

70
00:04:09,200 --> 00:04:10,267
Yes, ma'am.

71
00:04:15,867 --> 00:04:17,367
Why am I not yet released?

72
00:04:17,500 --> 00:04:19,400
We're doing everything we can.

73
00:04:20,033 --> 00:04:22,900
But we don't have
any connections in the NCIA.

74
00:04:23,033 --> 00:04:25,467
Don't worry,
we'll get you out of here.

75
00:04:25,600 --> 00:04:27,100
They caught Mr. Chan.

76
00:04:27,233 --> 00:04:29,733
He can throw us under
the bus anytime!

77
00:04:29,900 --> 00:04:32,700
The plan was to
eliminate him, but...

78
00:04:32,833 --> 00:04:34,300
Lucas couldn't do it.

79
00:04:34,433 --> 00:04:36,333
Lucas was even shot.

80
00:04:36,467 --> 00:04:38,967
Lucas was shot?!
Who did it?!

81
00:04:39,867 --> 00:04:41,333
I'm sure the guy I encountered

82
00:04:41,467 --> 00:04:43,633
has something to do with this.
Have you found him yet?

83
00:04:43,767 --> 00:04:44,867
[DEBORAH SIGHS]

84
00:04:45,000 --> 00:04:46,767
Arturo's searching for him.

85
00:04:47,700 --> 00:04:50,367
He better hide
once I find out who he is.

86
00:04:50,500 --> 00:04:52,900
For now, while we still
don't know who he is,

87
00:04:53,033 --> 00:04:55,167
I'll make sure Mr. Chan
keeps quiet.

88
00:04:57,167 --> 00:04:58,300
Do it, son.

89
00:05:04,200 --> 00:05:05,200
I'll count to three.

90
00:05:05,333 --> 00:05:07,833
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC PLAYING]

91
00:05:07,967 --> 00:05:09,133
Get your guns out!

92
00:05:11,200 --> 00:05:12,167
One!

93
00:05:15,400 --> 00:05:16,300
Two!

94
00:05:16,433 --> 00:05:23,367
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

95
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:27,800
- Three!
- Wait, Gabo! Wait!

96
00:05:28,500 --> 00:05:30,367
I-I'm not here for you.

97
00:05:31,500 --> 00:05:32,933
We're just trying
to make a living!

98
00:05:33,067 --> 00:05:37,200
We won't fight you, Gabo.
I know you have firearms.

99
00:05:37,367 --> 00:05:38,867
Believe me, Gabo.

100
00:05:39,000 --> 00:05:40,833
Ever since you defeated me...

101
00:05:40,967 --> 00:05:42,833
I never considered
taking revenge!

102
00:05:42,967 --> 00:05:46,700
I thought about our childhood.
Do you remember that?

103
00:05:47,733 --> 00:05:51,000
We were inseparable!
We worked together!

104
00:05:51,133 --> 00:05:53,100
You know, I even helped you!

105
00:05:53,233 --> 00:05:56,133
I hope you don't forget
those days, Gabo!

106
00:05:57,500 --> 00:05:59,733
Gabo, I'm sorry.

107
00:06:01,667 --> 00:06:03,333
I'll let you have this.

108
00:06:03,467 --> 00:06:06,400
If you want, you can bury him.

109
00:06:07,400 --> 00:06:09,033
I-I won't mess with him anymore.

110
00:06:09,833 --> 00:06:10,933
Django.

111
00:06:12,200 --> 00:06:14,467
If I hear that you're still
causing trouble here,

112
00:06:14,600 --> 00:06:15,833
I'll make sure...

113
00:06:16,900 --> 00:06:17,967
that tomorrow...

114
00:06:19,367 --> 00:06:20,800
...you'll be in a coffin.

115
00:06:21,700 --> 00:06:22,833
Okay, Gabo.

116
00:06:24,200 --> 00:06:25,400
Go bury your dad.

117
00:06:25,533 --> 00:06:27,300
- Let's go!
- Let's go, let's go!

118
00:06:27,433 --> 00:06:34,400
[SUSPENSEFUL MUSIC CONTINUES]

119
00:06:37,633 --> 00:06:38,633
[TOLITS GRUNTS]

120
00:06:38,767 --> 00:06:40,733
I thought we were going
to fight them.

121
00:06:40,900 --> 00:06:44,367
I was going to use up
all these bullets on Django.

122
00:06:44,500 --> 00:06:46,133
Good thing I controlled myself.

123
00:06:47,600 --> 00:06:51,000
They should be grateful
my head's clear.

124
00:06:51,133 --> 00:06:53,967
They're lucky.
If I used my shotgun...

125
00:06:54,100 --> 00:06:56,267
[IMITATES A GUN]
...they'd be dead.

126
00:06:57,233 --> 00:06:59,067
[TEKLA] You guys, stop it!

127
00:06:59,200 --> 00:07:01,533
You're all so arrogant
when the enemy's gone!

128
00:07:01,667 --> 00:07:03,967
You should be grateful
Django didn't do anything,

129
00:07:04,100 --> 00:07:06,500
or else we'd be the ones dead!
You're not using your heads.

130
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,767
Man, that got me so nervous!

131
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:11,367
Good thing Django
didn't come back,

132
00:07:11,500 --> 00:07:14,800
or else we're all dead!
They even have firearms!

133
00:07:14,967 --> 00:07:16,800
Gabo, Gabo.

134
00:07:16,933 --> 00:07:19,300
Thank you so much
for helping us.

135
00:07:19,433 --> 00:07:22,100
Gabo. Thank you, thank you.

136
00:07:22,833 --> 00:07:24,600
I can finally bury my husband.

137
00:07:28,200 --> 00:07:32,400
[WOMAN WHIMPERING]

138
00:07:32,533 --> 00:07:38,067
[SOMBER MUSIC PLAYING]

139
00:07:38,200 --> 00:07:39,433
Poor Sir Freddo.

140
00:07:39,567 --> 00:07:41,700
Those bastards
really are heartless.

141
00:07:47,100 --> 00:07:48,600
[MONEY RUSTLING]

142
00:07:48,767 --> 00:07:49,800
Miss Lourdes...

143
00:07:50,500 --> 00:07:53,833
- Please excuse our offering.
- Thank you so much, Gabo.

144
00:07:53,967 --> 00:07:55,867
I hope you can finally bury
Sir Freddo.

145
00:07:56,000 --> 00:07:58,133
Thank you, Gabo. Thank you.

146
00:07:58,767 --> 00:08:00,467
- Let's go.
- [TEKLA] Come on.

147
00:08:01,200 --> 00:08:02,567
Stop playing!

148
00:08:03,167 --> 00:08:04,767
[BINOY] Move aside, move aside.

149
00:08:04,900 --> 00:08:07,067
[INDISTINCT CONVERSATION]

150
00:08:07,200 --> 00:08:08,733
[OLI] Boss, take a look at this.

151
00:08:08,867 --> 00:08:10,233
Don't be embarrassed, Salvador.
Come here!

152
00:08:10,367 --> 00:08:11,467
That's so good, boss.

153
00:08:11,967 --> 00:08:13,300
[SALVADOR] That's the video
I bought.

154
00:08:13,433 --> 00:08:15,300
And there's the man
who saved me.

155
00:08:15,433 --> 00:08:18,400
- He was so brave, boss!
- [OLI] That guy's amazing!

156
00:08:18,533 --> 00:08:20,100
Don't think of him as the star.

157
00:08:20,233 --> 00:08:22,533
I mean, does he pull up
our ratings?

158
00:08:22,700 --> 00:08:25,467
[OLI] Boss is right.
Dude, you're the star.

159
00:08:25,600 --> 00:08:28,300
[ARNEL] This is so good.
We can use this!

160
00:08:28,433 --> 00:08:30,433
[SALVADOR] Boss, I'm the victim.

161
00:08:30,567 --> 00:08:34,400
My image might get ruined
from all that flimsy action.

162
00:08:34,533 --> 00:08:36,433
Dude, stop acting like
you're not in media.

163
00:08:36,567 --> 00:08:41,367
Let's show the people
what they want to see.

164
00:08:42,467 --> 00:08:44,667
[SALVADOR] That man
is the brave and helpful one.

165
00:08:45,700 --> 00:08:48,433
Gabo knocked down the muggers.

166
00:08:50,533 --> 00:08:52,200
I'm just a victim.

167
00:09:02,167 --> 00:09:03,100
Attorney.

168
00:09:07,867 --> 00:09:10,933
If only we had a connection
from the inside...

169
00:09:11,600 --> 00:09:13,833
We wouldn't have
these problems anymore.

170
00:09:13,967 --> 00:09:15,233
Mariano...

171
00:09:15,967 --> 00:09:17,733
The more you look,

172
00:09:17,867 --> 00:09:22,867
the more
our potential allies hide.

173
00:09:24,433 --> 00:09:27,533
If only we had an ally
from the higher-ups.

174
00:09:27,700 --> 00:09:29,667
[PENSIVE MUSIC PLAYING]

175
00:09:29,800 --> 00:09:32,333
Maybe you don't have
to look up.

176
00:09:33,767 --> 00:09:35,500
They're probably just close by.

177
00:09:36,133 --> 00:09:43,100
[PENSIVE MUSIC CONTINUES]

178
00:09:45,933 --> 00:09:46,933
[GATES CREAK]

179
00:09:50,300 --> 00:09:52,633
[KEYS JANGLING]

180
00:09:52,767 --> 00:09:55,067
- [LOCK CLANGING]
- [KEYS JANGLING]

181
00:09:55,200 --> 00:09:58,567
[HANDCUFFS CLANKING]

182
00:09:58,700 --> 00:10:05,667
[MUSIC TURNS TENSE]

183
00:10:08,133 --> 00:10:09,200
[MR. CHAN EXHALES]

184
00:10:10,567 --> 00:10:11,933
Who's your visitor?

185
00:10:15,733 --> 00:10:17,133
Why would you like to know?

186
00:10:17,267 --> 00:10:19,633
I want to know!
We're partners, right?

187
00:10:19,767 --> 00:10:21,733
Are we really allies, Mr. Chan?

188
00:10:21,867 --> 00:10:23,533
Or do you want to rat me out
to save yourself?

189
00:10:23,667 --> 00:10:25,033
I don't know
what you are saying!

190
00:10:25,167 --> 00:10:26,967
Didn't you tell anything
to the NCIA?

191
00:10:27,100 --> 00:10:28,600
Are you threatening me, Victor?!

192
00:10:28,733 --> 00:10:30,600
I told you mouth shut,
no talk!

193
00:10:30,733 --> 00:10:33,333
Why are you mad?
Did you snitch to the NCIA?

194
00:10:33,467 --> 00:10:34,400
No, no!

195
00:10:34,567 --> 00:10:36,967
- [MR. CHAN GROANING]
- [VICTOR GRUNTING]

196
00:10:37,100 --> 00:10:38,100
Stop that!

197
00:10:38,833 --> 00:10:40,133
[POLICE] Call for help!

198
00:10:40,733 --> 00:10:41,767
[OBJECT CLANGS]

199
00:10:43,167 --> 00:10:44,067
[POLICE] Stop that!

200
00:10:44,200 --> 00:10:46,533
[BOTH GRUNTING]

201
00:10:46,667 --> 00:10:49,300
- Hey! Stop that! Stop!
- Hey!

202
00:10:49,433 --> 00:10:50,867
[MR. CHAN GROANING]

203
00:10:52,033 --> 00:10:57,967
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

204
00:10:58,100 --> 00:10:59,033
[GATE CREAKS]

205
00:10:59,167 --> 00:11:02,300
[LOCK CLANGING]

206
00:11:03,567 --> 00:11:10,533
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

207
00:11:15,167 --> 00:11:16,433
Salvador,

208
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:17,967
listen to me, alright?

209
00:11:18,100 --> 00:11:21,333
No matter what kind
of story it is,

210
00:11:21,467 --> 00:11:23,167
you should be able
to manipulate it

211
00:11:23,300 --> 00:11:24,733
to be in your favor.

212
00:11:24,867 --> 00:11:28,833
That's the key for your
popularity to skyrocket.

213
00:11:28,967 --> 00:11:30,667
[STIRRING MUSIC PLAYING]

214
00:11:30,800 --> 00:11:32,833
This will be our pilot episode
for your show.

215
00:11:32,967 --> 00:11:35,767
We'll make it look like
someone tried to kill you.

216
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:37,533
This better be true, Salvador.

217
00:11:37,667 --> 00:11:40,267
Then, let's say that you
beat those people up.

218
00:11:40,400 --> 00:11:41,800
Wait, boss, hold it right there.

219
00:11:41,967 --> 00:11:43,167
You beat them up.

220
00:11:43,300 --> 00:11:44,667
- But I didn't--
- Yes, you did!

221
00:11:44,800 --> 00:11:46,700
- Alright, I did!
- That's it!

222
00:11:46,833 --> 00:11:48,833
They were no match for you!

223
00:11:48,967 --> 00:11:50,633
Now, you look tough.

224
00:11:50,967 --> 00:11:53,133
Now, you're the hero!

225
00:11:53,367 --> 00:11:54,467
Sounds fantastic.

226
00:11:56,233 --> 00:11:57,900
[ISOBEL] Okay, excuse me, Pinky.

227
00:11:58,033 --> 00:11:58,967
Hi!

228
00:11:59,100 --> 00:12:00,333
General!

229
00:12:00,800 --> 00:12:02,333
Oh, honey!

230
00:12:02,600 --> 00:12:05,033
- General's here.
- Oh, yes! You're early.

231
00:12:05,167 --> 00:12:06,967
Thanks for joining us.
Glad you could make it.

232
00:12:07,100 --> 00:12:08,233
- Vic!
- Evening, General!

233
00:12:08,367 --> 00:12:09,300
Good evening!

234
00:12:09,433 --> 00:12:10,800
What did we miss, General?

235
00:12:10,933 --> 00:12:11,767
Miss?

236
00:12:11,900 --> 00:12:13,467
A lot! Come, take a seat.

237
00:12:13,600 --> 00:12:15,533
Okay. Please, come in.

238
00:12:15,700 --> 00:12:16,933
- Hi!
- [WOMAN] General, hi!

239
00:12:17,067 --> 00:12:18,267
Good evening.

240
00:12:18,400 --> 00:12:19,567
Hello!

241
00:12:20,033 --> 00:12:21,533
I was just telling them

242
00:12:21,667 --> 00:12:23,267
how I got even more blessings

243
00:12:23,400 --> 00:12:26,267
ever since I purchased
Ginintuang Lupa.

244
00:12:26,400 --> 00:12:30,900
The moment Ricardo saw
the potential of the property,

245
00:12:31,033 --> 00:12:32,467
he purchased it right away!

246
00:12:32,600 --> 00:12:34,400
Yes, we are so blessed!

247
00:12:34,533 --> 00:12:35,433
- Yes!
- Yes!

248
00:12:35,567 --> 00:12:37,900
- It's a good investment!
- It is.

249
00:12:38,033 --> 00:12:39,533
But Ricardo,

250
00:12:40,333 --> 00:12:42,233
the demolition
of Ginintuang Lupa

251
00:12:42,367 --> 00:12:43,667
is still making a lot of noise.

252
00:12:44,733 --> 00:12:46,100
Well, that will pass.

253
00:12:46,500 --> 00:12:49,200
I mean, the complaining
of informal settlers

254
00:12:49,367 --> 00:12:50,800
when you try to take
your property

255
00:12:50,933 --> 00:12:52,233
isn't new to us anyway.

256
00:12:52,367 --> 00:12:53,900
Which doesn't belong to them
by the way.

257
00:12:54,033 --> 00:12:56,133
- That's right.
- One way or another,

258
00:12:56,267 --> 00:12:58,067
those informal settlers

259
00:12:58,200 --> 00:12:59,933
will have to leave that place!

260
00:13:00,067 --> 00:13:02,800
Oh, I wish they'd just flee
the place on their own

261
00:13:02,933 --> 00:13:06,600
so that we don't have to swat
those flies away anymore!

262
00:13:06,733 --> 00:13:08,233
[LAUGHTER]

263
00:13:08,367 --> 00:13:11,933
But Ricardo, how's
the development going?

264
00:13:12,067 --> 00:13:13,600
It's a waste of your time
and money

265
00:13:13,733 --> 00:13:16,367
until you don't make use
of that land.

266
00:13:16,500 --> 00:13:17,700
That's true, Vic.

267
00:13:17,833 --> 00:13:20,233
But, you know,
to be honest,

268
00:13:21,400 --> 00:13:24,000
I believe this is one
of my best investments.

269
00:13:24,133 --> 00:13:25,567
- Mm-hmm.
- You know,

270
00:13:25,700 --> 00:13:28,267
for now we're doing
the finishing touches

271
00:13:28,400 --> 00:13:30,967
and then we'll be opening it up
to future investors.

272
00:13:31,100 --> 00:13:32,033
Now,

273
00:13:32,167 --> 00:13:34,500
if you saved up some money

274
00:13:34,633 --> 00:13:37,467
or if you want
to be part of a...

275
00:13:37,600 --> 00:13:39,267
wise investment,

276
00:13:39,400 --> 00:13:43,567
join me. I can assure you,
my project won't fail you.

277
00:13:43,700 --> 00:13:46,200
- Yes, it's a good investment.
- [GUESTS CHATTERING]

278
00:13:46,333 --> 00:13:48,900
[ISOBEL] I'm telling you,
I saw the place already.

279
00:13:49,033 --> 00:13:50,933
Don't just keep those money.

280
00:13:51,067 --> 00:13:53,000
[ISOBEL] You should invest
in us already.

281
00:13:53,133 --> 00:13:55,367
[CLICKS TONGUE] You know,
[GROANS]

282
00:13:55,733 --> 00:13:57,133
- [DOOR CLOSES]
- [JACKET RUSTLES]

283
00:13:58,233 --> 00:14:00,300
my life will actually be
in danger

284
00:14:00,433 --> 00:14:02,433
with everything that Boss Arnel
is making me do.

285
00:14:02,567 --> 00:14:05,933
I just can't stomach that we're
fabricating the truth.

286
00:14:06,067 --> 00:14:07,367
Dude, that's what
the boss likes.

287
00:14:07,500 --> 00:14:09,833
He knows what the masses wants.

288
00:14:10,533 --> 00:14:12,733
They'll think you're a coward.

289
00:14:12,967 --> 00:14:15,067
And you'll return
to how it was before.

290
00:14:16,100 --> 00:14:17,633
And if that's what you want,

291
00:14:18,067 --> 00:14:19,533
you'll go back to zero.

292
00:14:19,667 --> 00:14:22,200
Of course I'm not going
to waste this opportunity.

293
00:14:22,333 --> 00:14:24,567
- As you should! [LAUGHING]
- Hey, watch it.

294
00:14:24,700 --> 00:14:27,033
My bad. I know, I know.

295
00:14:27,167 --> 00:14:30,067
We'll definitely
get a raise now!

296
00:14:30,633 --> 00:14:32,000
Come on, Salvador,

297
00:14:32,367 --> 00:14:33,800
if you don't do this,

298
00:14:33,933 --> 00:14:35,700
you'll go back to how you were.

299
00:14:35,833 --> 00:14:36,700
Poor as hell.

300
00:14:36,833 --> 00:14:39,733
Oh, Oli, I am not poor.

301
00:14:39,867 --> 00:14:42,433
Sir, Mr. Chan was almost killed
by Victor Zafra.

302
00:14:42,567 --> 00:14:43,733
- Are you sure?
- Yes, sir.

303
00:14:43,867 --> 00:14:45,367
We've already put them
in separate cells.

304
00:14:45,500 --> 00:14:47,400
[TENSE MUSIC PLAYING]

305
00:14:47,533 --> 00:14:48,733
[DOOR OPENS]

306
00:14:50,067 --> 00:14:51,833
Victor tried to kill me!

307
00:14:51,967 --> 00:14:53,667
My life is in danger!

308
00:14:54,100 --> 00:14:57,867
I don't think you know just what
kind of man Victor Zafra is.

309
00:14:58,567 --> 00:15:00,100
They will not stop...

310
00:15:00,733 --> 00:15:01,900
until you're dead.

311
00:15:02,067 --> 00:15:04,267
So do something! Protect me!

312
00:15:04,533 --> 00:15:05,600
I have my rights!

313
00:15:05,733 --> 00:15:07,767
If you want to live,

314
00:15:07,900 --> 00:15:09,667
cooperate with us.

315
00:15:09,800 --> 00:15:12,933
Be a state witness
against Victor Zaffra.

316
00:15:13,067 --> 00:15:15,567
We'll protect you
under witness protection

317
00:15:15,700 --> 00:15:19,333
but you have to tell us
everything you know.

318
00:15:19,467 --> 00:15:22,833
Until that syndicate
is not dissolved,

319
00:15:23,667 --> 00:15:25,100
you're not safe.

320
00:15:25,233 --> 00:15:29,067
You are not a free man
right now.

321
00:15:30,300 --> 00:15:31,800
But you are free...

322
00:15:33,067 --> 00:15:35,533
to choose your fate.

323
00:15:35,700 --> 00:15:39,867
[TENSE MUSIC CONTINUES]

324
00:15:40,000 --> 00:15:42,700
[CAR DOORS OPENING]

325
00:15:43,433 --> 00:15:44,400
[CAR DOORS CLOSING]

326
00:15:44,533 --> 00:15:45,600
- [KAREN] It still hurts.
- [SEBASTIAN CHUCKLES]

327
00:15:45,733 --> 00:15:46,700
[KAREN] Sorry, sir.

328
00:15:47,800 --> 00:15:49,167
Alright, listen up.

329
00:15:49,900 --> 00:15:53,167
I'd like to remind everyone.
We're here to have a good time.

330
00:15:53,600 --> 00:15:55,033
Okay? Let's have fun.

331
00:15:55,267 --> 00:15:56,733
Let's forget about everything
that happened.

332
00:15:56,867 --> 00:15:58,600
It's just really hard
to accept it.

333
00:15:59,267 --> 00:16:01,133
[SEBASTIAN] And that's why
we're here!

334
00:16:01,267 --> 00:16:02,867
Let's just drink it all away,
okay?

335
00:16:03,300 --> 00:16:05,767
- How about it, Sam?
-I'm fine. Don't worry about me.

336
00:16:06,100 --> 00:16:07,600
Don't let me ruin your night.

337
00:16:07,733 --> 00:16:09,133
- Okay.
- Ma'am Sam,

338
00:16:09,300 --> 00:16:12,333
if you want to rest, we can do
this some other time.

339
00:16:12,467 --> 00:16:15,500
[RALLOS] You'll just go crazy
thinking about it.

340
00:16:15,633 --> 00:16:17,933
Let's just go inside. Come on!

341
00:16:18,067 --> 00:16:19,900
- Let's go then!
- Woohoo!

342
00:16:20,033 --> 00:16:21,133
Let's go!

343
00:16:22,467 --> 00:16:24,333
- Hey, Ron!
- Sir Seb!

344
00:16:24,467 --> 00:16:26,900
- Your table's ready.
- Very good!

345
00:16:27,033 --> 00:16:28,767
- Lead the way.
- Good.

346
00:16:28,900 --> 00:16:30,800
Yes, yes, yo!

347
00:16:30,933 --> 00:16:33,067
[ROCK MUSIC PLAYING]

348
00:16:33,200 --> 00:16:35,067
[RALLOS] Good job!

349
00:16:35,200 --> 00:16:36,700
- Oh, Karen, sit here.
- Oh.

350
00:16:36,833 --> 00:16:38,633
- So it's comfortable for you.
- Here, Sam.

351
00:16:38,767 --> 00:16:42,900
[ROCK MUSIC CONTINUES]

352
00:16:43,067 --> 00:16:44,900
- [BINOY] Whoa!
- [TEKLA] This is the place?!

353
00:16:45,033 --> 00:16:47,500
You should've told me!
I would've worn my heels.

354
00:16:47,633 --> 00:16:48,533
Oh, you!

355
00:16:48,667 --> 00:16:50,100
Let's go back
to the diner then.

356
00:16:50,233 --> 00:16:52,833
- Whoa, hey! I'm just joking!
- No way!

357
00:16:52,967 --> 00:16:54,167
Come on, Gabo.

358
00:16:54,300 --> 00:16:55,833
It's not everyday that we get
to drink at a place like this.

359
00:16:55,967 --> 00:16:57,267
Let's make the most of it
plus...

360
00:16:57,400 --> 00:16:58,733
you got 10,000 pesos anyway.

361
00:16:58,867 --> 00:17:01,400
Finally! A meal
that's not pagpag!

362
00:17:01,533 --> 00:17:03,800
- [LAUGHS]
- Gabo, I'm parched!

363
00:17:03,933 --> 00:17:05,967
I'm finally getting some booze!

364
00:17:06,100 --> 00:17:07,667
- Cold beer!
- [LAUGHTER]

365
00:17:07,800 --> 00:17:09,933
As for me, Gabo, I'm starving.

366
00:17:10,267 --> 00:17:12,467
As if you aren't all the time!

367
00:17:12,600 --> 00:17:14,933
Even stale and burnt rice
end up in your stomach!

368
00:17:15,100 --> 00:17:16,400
Don't worry, guys.

369
00:17:16,733 --> 00:17:18,867
I'll feed you real good grub!

370
00:17:19,000 --> 00:17:21,467
And I'll make sure you'll drown
in booze tonight.

371
00:17:21,600 --> 00:17:25,933
[LAUGHTER, CHEERING]

372
00:17:26,067 --> 00:17:27,333
Looks like there's a lot
of people today.

373
00:17:27,633 --> 00:17:28,833
Show us how you'll throw up.

374
00:17:28,967 --> 00:17:30,667
- [FAKE GAGS]
- [FAKE GAGS]

375
00:17:30,800 --> 00:17:32,700
[OVERLAPPING CHATTER]

376
00:17:32,833 --> 00:17:34,767
- Oh.
- Table for how many, sir?

377
00:17:35,100 --> 00:17:36,067
Uh, for seven.

378
00:17:36,200 --> 00:17:43,133
[UPBEAT MUSIC PLAYING]

379
00:17:51,067 --> 00:17:53,600
That bastard Delgado
is way too arrogant.

380
00:17:54,467 --> 00:17:56,400
Who does he think he is?!

381
00:17:56,400 --> 00:17:59,767
Back in my day,
he was just a low-level agent!

382
00:18:00,700 --> 00:18:03,600
I suspect he's targeting Victor

383
00:18:03,600 --> 00:18:05,200
because he knows he's my son.

384
00:18:05,800 --> 00:18:07,900
That bastard will get
his payback soon.

385
00:18:08,467 --> 00:18:09,967
- Arturo.
- Ma'am.

386
00:18:11,233 --> 00:18:15,067
Dig into Director Delgado's
background.

387
00:18:15,067 --> 00:18:17,833
I'm sure we can use
something against him.

388
00:18:17,833 --> 00:18:19,167
Yes, ma'am.
I'll take care of it.

389
00:18:19,167 --> 00:18:21,100
Ma.
How's Victor doing?

390
00:18:21,100 --> 00:18:22,333
He's miserable!

391
00:18:22,967 --> 00:18:24,567
He doesn't belong there.

392
00:18:25,433 --> 00:18:29,100
Ma, we need to get Victor
out of there!

393
00:18:29,100 --> 00:18:33,767
If we need to storm the NCIA
to break him out,

394
00:18:34,267 --> 00:18:35,267
I'll do it, Ma!

395
00:18:35,267 --> 00:18:38,200
Lucas, calm down!

396
00:18:38,200 --> 00:18:41,233
This is not the time
for you to be rash.

397
00:18:42,033 --> 00:18:43,500
You have to think.

398
00:18:44,200 --> 00:18:45,833
And think smart.

399
00:18:48,267 --> 00:18:50,233
[STAFF] I'm sorry, sir.
There's no space inside anymore.

400
00:18:50,233 --> 00:18:51,900
However, there are
tables available outside.

401
00:18:51,900 --> 00:18:53,700
- What?
- But it's hot here!

402
00:18:53,700 --> 00:18:55,600
- We just cleared a table.
- There's no air conditioning.

403
00:18:55,633 --> 00:18:57,600
[BINOY] We should've stayed
at home!

404
00:18:57,600 --> 00:18:59,967
Cut the dramatics, as if
you aren't used to the heat.

405
00:18:59,967 --> 00:19:02,100
[TOLITS] Fine.
At least the food is good.

406
00:19:02,100 --> 00:19:04,167
Don't worry.
The food here is good.

407
00:19:04,167 --> 00:19:05,800
[TOLITS] C'mon,
we should order.

408
00:19:05,800 --> 00:19:07,267
Gabo.

409
00:19:07,267 --> 00:19:08,600
Thank you.

410
00:19:08,933 --> 00:19:11,567
We know your cut from
that gig was small,

411
00:19:11,567 --> 00:19:13,667
but you still managed
to treat us.

412
00:19:14,367 --> 00:19:15,933
C'mon, guys.

413
00:19:15,933 --> 00:19:17,500
I'm actually the one feeling
embarrassed around you guys.

414
00:19:18,533 --> 00:19:20,500
I wasn't even able to share
my cut with you guys

415
00:19:20,500 --> 00:19:21,800
from my second mission.

416
00:19:22,300 --> 00:19:23,833
So even if it's
just ten thousand,

417
00:19:23,833 --> 00:19:25,300
lat least I was able
to make it up to you guys.

418
00:19:25,300 --> 00:19:26,633
[IPE] It's alright, Gabo.

419
00:19:26,633 --> 00:19:29,400
We weren't with you
on your second mission.

420
00:19:29,433 --> 00:19:32,733
Our agreement was that if
we joined you on the mission,

421
00:19:32,733 --> 00:19:35,933
we get a fifty percent cut
of your earnings.

422
00:19:36,567 --> 00:19:38,933
- [BONG] What was your mission?
- [BINOY] Was it dangerous?

423
00:19:38,933 --> 00:19:42,933
[TOLITS] We went up against
big shots on our first mission.

424
00:19:42,933 --> 00:19:44,900
[DABOY] You're right.
They had big guns.

425
00:19:46,200 --> 00:19:47,267
You know what,

426
00:19:48,367 --> 00:19:50,267
my second mission
was even harder.

427
00:19:52,267 --> 00:19:54,233
I've had to deal with
bigger syndicates.

428
00:19:55,000 --> 00:19:57,233
Even the NCIA was involved.

429
00:19:57,233 --> 00:19:58,500
The NCIA was there?!

430
00:19:58,500 --> 00:20:01,467
They were also there
on our first mission, right?

431
00:20:01,500 --> 00:20:03,333
Yeah, they were
the ones who fired first.

432
00:20:03,333 --> 00:20:05,467
That's why there was
a shootout inside the bar.

433
00:20:06,033 --> 00:20:07,433
Hey, wait a minute.

434
00:20:07,833 --> 00:20:09,833
Thank God your mission
was a success.

435
00:20:09,833 --> 00:20:11,400
[SEBASTIAN] We'll have
seven beers for now.

436
00:20:11,967 --> 00:20:13,133
Very good, very good.
Thank you.

437
00:20:13,600 --> 00:20:15,600
[CASTOR SIGHS] We really went
through a lot, didn't we?

438
00:20:16,067 --> 00:20:17,200
I couldn't even imagine

439
00:20:17,200 --> 00:20:20,000
that we went up against
a big syndicate.

440
00:20:20,000 --> 00:20:22,167
[KAREN] I almost died!

441
00:20:22,167 --> 00:20:23,467
[ROBERT] Seems like
they were ready for us.

442
00:20:23,467 --> 00:20:26,467
This group is definitely bigger
than Victor Zafra's crew.

443
00:20:26,933 --> 00:20:28,633
[BORROMEO] What matters
now is that

444
00:20:28,633 --> 00:20:30,600
they didn't get
the upper hand on us.

445
00:20:30,600 --> 00:20:32,267
We have Mr. Chan.

446
00:20:33,000 --> 00:20:34,433
[GABO] When
they started fighting,

447
00:20:34,433 --> 00:20:37,767
that's when I sneaked in
to get the gold.

448
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:39,733
What? Did you say gold?

449
00:20:39,733 --> 00:20:41,100
Do you have the gold?

450
00:20:41,100 --> 00:20:42,833
How much gold
do you have, Gabo?

451
00:20:42,833 --> 00:20:44,567
That must've been worth
a lot of money!

452
00:20:44,567 --> 00:20:46,700
You can say that again.

453
00:20:46,700 --> 00:20:48,867
We saw it at the bar!

454
00:20:48,867 --> 00:20:50,200
- [TOLITS] Was it a lot?
- Yes.

455
00:20:50,200 --> 00:20:52,500
They only gave you
one hundred thousand?

456
00:20:52,800 --> 00:20:53,867
[TEKLA] He's right.

457
00:20:55,033 --> 00:20:57,033
Two hundred thousand pesos.

458
00:20:57,033 --> 00:20:59,400
But one hundred thousand
of that was a bonus

459
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:00,600
for returning the gold.

460
00:21:01,367 --> 00:21:02,267
[SAM] That's the thing.

461
00:21:02,767 --> 00:21:04,967
We already caught Mr. Chan,

462
00:21:05,967 --> 00:21:07,567
but we ended up
in this situation.

463
00:21:07,567 --> 00:21:10,567
[RALLOS] Ma'am Pia has
her eyes on you, Ma'am Sam.

464
00:21:10,600 --> 00:21:12,467
Apart from that,
Sir Delgado is pissed at you.

465
00:21:12,467 --> 00:21:13,700
Don't worry about that.

466
00:21:13,700 --> 00:21:15,600
I will take care
of all of you.

467
00:21:15,600 --> 00:21:17,367
I'll talk to Delgado.

468
00:21:17,833 --> 00:21:18,833
It'll be fine.

469
00:21:18,833 --> 00:21:19,933
[BONG] That's a shame,
Gabo.

470
00:21:20,567 --> 00:21:21,800
You should've run away
with the gold.

471
00:21:21,800 --> 00:21:23,933
You would've gotten out
of Ginintuang Lupa by now.

472
00:21:23,933 --> 00:21:25,200
You and your whole family.

473
00:21:25,200 --> 00:21:28,233
C'mon, Gabo isn't like you!

474
00:21:28,233 --> 00:21:31,400
Even if he's like that,
his conscience is clean.

475
00:21:32,400 --> 00:21:33,900
[IPE] I respect you, Gabo.

476
00:21:34,533 --> 00:21:36,033
You're so different from us.

477
00:21:36,033 --> 00:21:38,967
If that were me, I would've
run away with the gold.

478
00:21:39,900 --> 00:21:43,733
Gabo, what happened
to the NCIA?

479
00:21:43,767 --> 00:21:44,967
Did they recognize you?

480
00:21:46,467 --> 00:21:48,533
[KAREN] We'll definitely get
in trouble sooner or later.

481
00:21:48,533 --> 00:21:49,767
If Sam gets suspended,

482
00:21:49,767 --> 00:21:52,700
what if we get suspended
and get laid off from work too?

483
00:21:52,700 --> 00:21:56,100
That sounds nicer.
But what you did was illegal.

484
00:21:57,733 --> 00:22:00,267
They might be looking for you!
Don't drag us with you!

485
00:22:00,267 --> 00:22:01,367
They won't.

486
00:22:02,233 --> 00:22:05,200
They didn't see me because
I escaped right away.

487
00:22:05,200 --> 00:22:06,633
So don't worry.
We are safe.

488
00:22:06,633 --> 00:22:07,667
[TEKLA] That's right.

489
00:22:07,667 --> 00:22:09,833
I think it's best if we order.

490
00:22:10,200 --> 00:22:12,133
The waiter keeps
on ignoring me.

491
00:22:12,133 --> 00:22:13,600
I'm starving!

492
00:22:13,600 --> 00:22:15,133
[IPE] Waiter!

493
00:22:15,167 --> 00:22:16,733
[TOLITS] Where are they?

494
00:22:16,733 --> 00:22:19,033
[BINOY] The place is packed.
Maybe they're inside.

495
00:22:19,033 --> 00:22:22,567
It's fine.
I'll go to the bar to order.

496
00:22:22,567 --> 00:22:24,533
- [IPE] You don't have to.
- [TOLITS] Thank you!

497
00:22:24,533 --> 00:22:26,833
[BINOY] One ice-cold
beer, please.

498
00:22:26,833 --> 00:22:28,667
You've got some serious nerve.

499
00:22:28,667 --> 00:22:35,700
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

500
00:22:50,700 --> 00:22:57,667
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

501
00:23:20,600 --> 00:23:22,000
[ROMY] What do you plan,
Paquito?

502
00:23:22,833 --> 00:23:24,533
Want us
to beat him up ourselves?

503
00:23:24,667 --> 00:23:29,367
Let's wait for Umali's orders.

504
00:23:29,500 --> 00:23:33,800
[PHONE RINGING]

505
00:23:35,233 --> 00:23:37,600
- Hello?
- For pete's sake, Paquito.

506
00:23:37,733 --> 00:23:41,000
The job's so simple,
yet you still failed?

507
00:23:41,133 --> 00:23:44,333
The match isn't over, Umali.

508
00:23:44,467 --> 00:23:49,033
If you want, Romy and I
will finish it.

509
00:23:49,167 --> 00:23:52,400
Come out here
before I lose my patience!

510
00:23:52,533 --> 00:23:53,600
[LINE DROPS]

511
00:23:56,067 --> 00:23:57,000
[PHONE TURNS OFF]

512
00:23:58,767 --> 00:24:01,467
[UNSETTLING MUSIC PLAYING]

513
00:24:01,600 --> 00:24:03,833
Django, come with us.

514
00:24:03,967 --> 00:24:06,100
Explain to Umali what happened.

515
00:24:07,833 --> 00:24:14,733
[UNSETTLING MUSIC CONTINUES]

516
00:24:25,600 --> 00:24:32,533
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA"
BY JUAN KARLOS PLAYING]

517
00:24:47,567 --> 00:24:54,500
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

518
00:25:09,567 --> 00:25:16,467
["TUNAY NA LIGAYA" CONTINUES]

519
00:25:26,467 --> 00:25:27,933
<i> They did mug Salvador.</i>

520
00:25:28,067 --> 00:25:29,967
But that bastard became bolder.

521
00:25:30,100 --> 00:25:31,800
<i>Aren't you cops?
You can handle that!</i>

522
00:25:31,933 --> 00:25:33,500
<i>You know,
you reek of arrogance.</i>

523
00:25:33,633 --> 00:25:35,833
<i>You're too proud when
you're nothing like your father.</i>

524
00:25:36,000 --> 00:25:38,600
<i>Go on, shoot me!
Let's see how brave you are.</i>

525
00:25:38,733 --> 00:25:42,833
Challenge all those criminals,
and ask them how much they are!

526
00:25:42,967 --> 00:25:44,633
<i> Here comes</i>

527
00:25:44,767 --> 00:25:47,400
<i>- Salvador "The Vindicator"!
- Salvador "The Vindicator"!</i>

528
00:25:47,533 --> 00:25:49,367
<i> Bring it on!</i> [GROWLS]

529
00:25:50,400 --> 00:25:53,233
<i>You know, Sam, I was thinking,
why don't we go on vacation?</i>

530
00:25:53,367 --> 00:25:55,167
<i> Anywhere we can unwind!</i>

531
00:25:55,300 --> 00:25:57,400
<i>Somewhere far away
from our problems.</i>

532
00:25:57,533 --> 00:25:58,767
<i> Somewhere far away from here.</i>

533
00:25:58,900 --> 00:26:01,767
<i>I know you. You're the three
bastards from Chinatown.</i>

534
00:26:01,900 --> 00:26:05,233
<i>Why? Will you fight back?
Wanna taste my punch?</i>

535
00:26:05,367 --> 00:26:07,067
- [BLOW LANDS]
<i> - That's it?</i>

536
00:26:07,200 --> 00:26:09,033
- [BLOWS LANDING]
- [GRUNTING]

537
00:26:09,200 --> 00:26:11,800
<i>If they file a complaint
against us,</i>

538
00:26:11,933 --> 00:26:13,367
<i> we might end up suspended!</i>

539
00:26:13,500 --> 00:26:16,400
<i>- Gabo, help us!
- Some NCIA guys beat us up!</i>

540
00:26:16,533 --> 00:26:18,167
<i>We might be able
to catch up to them, Gabo!</i>

541
00:26:18,300 --> 00:26:19,867
<i>Come on, come on!
Let's catch up to them!</i>

542
00:26:20,000 --> 00:26:21,067
<i> Hurry!</i>
